WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.367
-Marlon Wayans!
-Thank you.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.801
-Looking good, bud.
-Thank you.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:06.834
-As always, looking good.
-I'm fangirling right now.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:09.067
I just got a peek
of Willem Dafoe.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.334
I didn't get to meet him,
but I got to see him.

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:13.334
-Yeah, that's all
you really need to do.

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:15.667
-He has, like, one of
the most distinct faces.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.067
-It's unbelievable.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.701
-Although, with the mustache,
he looks like

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:21.467
Professor Hinkle from
"Frosty the Snowman."

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:22.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.734
But he just always, like --

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:27.367
I knew he was Green Goblin
even with the mask on.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:30.467
He has a very distinct face.
-Yeah, you just knew it was him.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.234
-Like, even if he had played
Spider-Man with the mask,

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.601
he'd still be like...
-Yeah. You know.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.734
You look great, bud.
-Thank you, man.

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.334
-Is this true? You turned 50?

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:40.868
-Yeah, you know that Black
don't crack unless you smoke it.

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:42.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:43.767
-What are you talking about?

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:47.567
-Let's be clear, Jimmy.
I turned Black 50.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:49.400
[ Laughter ]
-What is Black 50?

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.400
-Oh, it's different
than white 50.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.934
It's, uh --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:55.934
Black 50 is like --
We, like, 25 in the face

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:58.400
and, like, 82 in the prostate.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.634
You know what I mean?

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:02.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:04.367
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:08.467
White 50 look like it hurt.
Oh, my God. Ohh!

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.734
I see my white friend's 50,
I just hug them like,

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:12.467
"You ain't gonna make it to 51."

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:14.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.367
-You got to celebrate it,
though, with your son.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:21.634
-I just celebrated his 21st,
which was awesome.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.901
-Is that right?
-Yeah, so, I flew in to Miami,

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:26.267
and we was gonna party all day.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.067
And, you know,
I was down for it.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:32.133
So I flew in, and we went
to Club 11 for breakfast,

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:34.267
which is a strip club, so...

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:35.667
That's how you want to spend 21.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:37.601
And then that night
we went to Live,

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:41.734
and I get a text from my son
at like 2:00

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:45.033
and he's like, "We out."

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.434
I was there
until 7:00 in the morning.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:49.801
I don't know
which one of us turned 50.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:53.267
-Kids don't want to
hang out late anymore.

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:55.200
-I don't know.
I'm like, "You ain't got no job.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.467
Why are you going home?"

00:01:57.467 --> 00:01:59.534
-That's wild, though.
That's crazy.

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:01.701
-Yes.
-You know what's interesting?

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.834
I just don't feel the need
to stay out that late anymore.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.267
-That's 'cause
you're rich, Jimmy.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.334
Uh...

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:10.767
Rich people just want to go to
sleep just to count their money.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.868
"I don't need to go out.
We'll bring out in."

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.601
-[ Laughs ] Bring out in.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:19.501
-Speaking of rich, listen.
I'm hosting -- I'm guest hosting

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:22.100
"The Daily Show,"
and I need a guest.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.467
And...

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.601
-What are you talking about?

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:29.567
-And I figure you owe me
like 12, right?

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:32.400
Because I come on this show
and I give you a break.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.167
You just be like --

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:36.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:37.901
And I just sit here,

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:41.734
and I blap, blap, blap,
blap, blap, blap.

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:43.734
Because some guests,
it's like pulling teeth.

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:45.634
You know what I mean?
I don't know how to do this.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.467
Your part -- I don't know
how to ask questions.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.167
I'll be like this --

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:50.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:53.300
[Snorts] "Yeah, give it up
for Marlon Wayans."

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.133
-What are you talking about?
-I need a guest.

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:58.234
So I need you to come
on "The Daily Show"

00:02:58.234 --> 00:02:59.501
and let me interview you.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.033
We don't know anything
about you.

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:04.033
I want to know why haven't you
let me come to the Hamptons.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.067
I want to know...

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:10.367
how come you hang with the
brother from the "Hamilton,"

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:12.801
but I can't be in a pool
with you?

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.367
What's up with that?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:16.968
-How do you know I was in a pool
with the dude from "Hamilton"?

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.067
-I was going to --

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:22.067
I was personally going to reach
out and talk to you, right,

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:24.901
and invite you on to be
my guest, but then I realized

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:28.367
I ain't got your number,
so what I did...

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.334
was I used this opportunity
to be like,

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.701
"Yo, Jimmy, come on
'The Daily Show.'

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:34.100
Let me holla at you."

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:43.133
-Marlon, I let "The Daily Show"
come to me.

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:44.868
-Ooh!

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.934
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:50.067
Ohh! Ohh!

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:53.634
Shots fired! Shots fired!
Ohh!

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.234
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.801
Shots fired!

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:59.334
Ooh!

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.000
That was good, Jimmy.
-That was not bad.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.133
-That was good. See, that's why
I wanted you as my guest.

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:05.734
I knew you had jokes.
They don't know.

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:07.567
See, you had to come
from behind the desk.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.133
Behind the desk,
it emasculates you.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:12.000
You come over here, and you
start doing jokes at people.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.067
[ Laughter ]
-Unbeliev--

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:16.601
What are they going to do?

00:04:16.601 --> 00:04:18.133
"The Daily Show." What are they
going to do with Marlon Wayans?

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:19.467
-I don't know.
Nail me to the seat.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.033
Because I don't know
how I'm-a sit down.

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.567
I'm not good at that.

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:24.434
-I can't see you behind a desk.
-I can't see me behind a desk.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.367
-Get rid of that desk.
-My teachers couldn't see me

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:28.300
behind a desk
'cause I was cutting class.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:32.734
-I want to talk to you about --
There's two things.

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:34.934
Well, first, let's just
talk about "God Loves Me."

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:36.467
-Yes.
-Congratulations on this.

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:37.701
-Thank you.

00:04:37.701 --> 00:04:38.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:41.501
-HBO Max.
-Yes.

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:43.467
-Why is it called
"God Loves Me"?

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:47.133
-Because I think
God loves all of us,

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:48.734
but he really loves me.

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:50.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.934
Because I feel like
cataclysmic things happen

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:57.033
in the world that have nothing
to do with you, per se,

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.667
but then you think about it,

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.734
and it has everything
to do with you.

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:03.300
And one of those events
to me was SlapGate.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:07.567
And when Chris Rock and Will
had that --

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:10.901
Yeah, when Will hit him,
life went like --

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:13.033
[Whooshing] for me.

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:17.100
Maybe Will hit him
that hard that I --

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.601
It changed my life,

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:21.367
and so I know Will,
Chris, and Jada,

00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:22.734
and I was just like,

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:24.801
"Yo, somebody got to
talk about this story

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:26.968
from a loving,
funny perspective."

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:29.067
And so I called it
"God Loves Me"

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:31.868
because that slap had nothing
to do with the three of them,

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:33.567
had everything to do with me.

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:35.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:37.567 --> 00:05:39.434
-I'm sorry. I'm so lost.

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:41.901
How did it have anything
to do with you?

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:43.734
-I don't know, but even -- Look.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:45.901
It's like -- Questlove.
Why is he everywhere?

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.934
And it ain't got nothing
to do with him?

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:50.267
He was right there like,
"Oh, my God!"

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:51.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:53.434
I seen the brother
clutch his pearls.

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.467
He said, "What?!"

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:57.434
-[ Laughs ] Pearls.
-But he's everywhere.

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:59.234
One night,
it was me, Dave Chappelle,

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:01.467
Chris Rock, all of us on stage.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:03.267
And I look on stage,
and I'm like,

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:05.834
"What the hell is Questlove
doing here?"

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:07.934
You look through history,
you are the Black Forrest Gump.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.067
He's gonna be...

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:12.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.067 --> 00:06:13.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:17.267
In classic pictures.
Him and Malcolm X by the window.

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:20.300
Like...

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.234
The Martin Luther King
assassination.

00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:24.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:26.400
-He's everywhere.
-Right.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.467
-January 6th at Pelosi's desk.

00:06:28.467 --> 00:06:30.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:33.734
-Oh, my -- Dude.

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:36.167
-Ohh!
-Ohh!

00:06:36.167 --> 00:06:37.534
-Shots fired!

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:40.868
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:44.067
-Dude. Good luck, "Daily Show."
You can't hold him down.

00:06:44.067 --> 00:06:45.634
Marlon Wayans, everybody.

00:06:45.634 --> 00:06:48.300
"Marlon Wayans: God Loves Me."
-Thank you.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.400
-"God Loves Me" premieres
Thursday on HBO Max.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.300
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

